content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent sample size calculation: 230 PFS events with 70% maturity implies 329 subjects, not 330, and 160 events is 69.6% not 70%",
      "page": 103,
      "quote": "With 230 PFS events, the study will have ~90% power ... The sample size is chosen to have 70% maturity realizing PFS events, which is approximately 330 subjects with 1:1 randomization ratio ... An IA is planned when approximately 70% (160) of the target PFS events have been observed",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contradictory statements about whether the trial can be terminated at PFS analyses",
      "page": 104,
      "quote": "As designed, the trial will not be terminated at PFS analyses and subjects will continue to be followed for OS data until the targeted number of events are reached, regardless of the OS analysis result at the PFS primary analysis",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent timing for OS primary analysis: text says 198 events expected at 3 months after PFS PA, but Table 9-1 says 22 months vs 19 months (3 months later) and also says OS at PFS PA triggered by 175 events, conflicting with text saying 175 events is for OS assessment at PFS PA or later",
      "page": 104,
      "quote": "The OS primary analysis will occur when at least 198 OS events (~60% maturity) have been observed, which is expected to be at approximately 3 months after PFS primary analysis ... Table 9-1: OS at PFS PA N.A. 19 months 175 OS events; OS PA N.A. 22 months 198 OS events",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of OS interim summary: text says 107 OS events (~32% maturity) but 107/330 is 32.4%, and later says 175 events (~53% maturity) but 175/330 is 53.0%, but the text also says 'at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events ... whichever is later' which contradicts Table 9-1 that says OS at PFS PA is triggered by 175 events",
      "page": 104,
      "quote": "an administrative interim summary for OS will be performed with approximately 107 OS events (~32% maturity) observed ... Otherwise, the OS will be assessed for superiority of AMG 510 over docetaxel at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events (~53% maturity) have been observed, whichever is later",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about whether PFS IA can serve as PA: Section 9.4.1.2 says 'If PFS early success is achieved in the IA, the IA will serve the purpose of PA of PFS' but Section 9.4.1.1 says 'the trial will not be terminated at PFS analyses' and Section 9.4.1.2 also says 'The PA of PFS will be event driven and will happen when approximately 230 PFS events are reached'",
      "page": 108,
      "quote": "If PFS early success is achieved in the IA, the IA will serve the purpose of PA of PFS. The PFS PA may be delayed to ensure that the enrollment is finished and the delayed PA will be triggered when the last randomized subject have had the opportunity to have at least 6 weeks of follow up.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of OS analysis timing: Section 9.4.1.1 says OS assessed at PFS PA or after 175 events, whichever later, but Table 9-1 says OS at PFS PA is triggered by 175 events, and Section 9.4.1.2 says PA for OS will occur when approximately 198 OS events have been reached, without mentioning the 175-event trigger",
      "page": 107,
      "quote": "Otherwise, the OS will be assessed for superiority of AMG 510 over docetaxel at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events (~53% maturity) have been observed, whichever is later.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of PFS analysis set: Section 9.3.1.1 says full analysis set used for primary and key secondary efficacy endpoints, but Section 9.4.2.2 says 'The PA of PFS will be based on BICR centrally assessed outcomes' and 'The primary comparison for PFS between treatment and control will use the log rank test stratified by randomization factors per IRT' - IRT is not defined and may be a typo for ICR?",
      "page": 109,
      "quote": "The primary comparison for PFS between treatment and control will use the log rank test stratified by randomization factors per IRT. The HR and its 95% CI will be estimated using a Cox proportional hazards model stratified by the randomization stratification factors per IRT.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of PRO endpoints: Section 9.1 lists 6 PRO hypotheses (dyspnea, cough, chest pain, physical functioning, global health status) but Section 9.4.2.1 says 'The inferential comparison for the endpoints of change from baseline over time to week 12 in symptoms of dyspnea ... physical functioning, global health status ... will be made through a mixed model for repeated measurement (MMRM). The inferential comparison for the endpoints of change from baseline over time to week 12 in symptoms of cough and chest pain ... will be made through generalized estimating equations (GEE) method' - this is consistent, but the multiple testing procedure in Section 9.1 says 'If all 3 hypotheses of PFS, OS, ORR are rejected, the next 3 endpoints ... will be tested using Holm’s procedure' and then 'If all 6 hypotheses listed above are rejected, the next 2 PRO endpoints will be tested' - but there are 6 PRO endpoints, not 3+2=5, so the count is wrong.",
      "page": 102,
      "quote": "If all 3 hypotheses of PFS, OS, ORR are rejected, the next 3 endpoints of change from baseline over time to week 12 in 3 lung cancer symptoms will be tested using Holm’s procedure ... If all 6 hypotheses listed above are rejected, the next 2 PRO endpoints will be tested using the Holm’s procedure",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of PRO analysis methods: Section 9.4.2.1 says cough and chest pain are measured by a single question from QLQ-LC13, but Section 9.1 says cough and chest pain are measured by QLQ-LC13 (not single question) and dyspnea is measured by a 4-item dyspnea domain from QLQ-C30 and QLQ-LC13, which is consistent, but the statistical section says 'change from baseline over time to week 12 in symptoms of cough and chest pain as measured by a single question from QLQ-LC13' - this is a minor inconsistency with the hypothesis section that doesn't specify single question.",
      "page": 109,
      "quote": "The inferential comparison for the endpoints of change from baseline over time to week 12 in symptoms of cough and chest pain as measured by a single question from QLQ-LC13 will be made through generalized estimating equations (GEE) method",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of OS analysis: Section 9.4.1.2 says 'The PA for OS will be event driven and will occur when approximately 198 OS events have been reached' but Section 9.4.1.1 says 'Otherwise, the OS will be assessed for superiority of AMG 510 over docetaxel at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events ... whichever is later' - this implies OS may be assessed at PFS PA with 175 events, but then the PA for OS is at 198 events, so there are two possible OS analyses, which is not clearly described.",
      "page": 108,
      "quote": "The PA for OS will be event driven and will occur when approximately 198 OS events have been reached.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of PFS analysis timing: Section 9.2 says 'The PA of PFS will occur when approximately 230 PFS events have been observed' and 'The PFS PA may be delayed to ensure that the enrollment is finished and the delayed PA will be triggered when the last randomized subject have had the opportunity to have at least 6 weeks of follow up.' But Section 9.4.1.2 says 'If PFS early success is achieved in the IA, the IA will serve the purpose of PA of PFS' - this is a contradiction because if IA is positive, the PA is at IA, not at 230 events.",
      "page": 103,
      "quote": "The PA of PFS will occur when approximately 230 PFS events have been observed.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent description of OS analysis: Section 9.2 says 'If PFS achieves statistical significance at the interim analysis, an administrative interim summary for OS will be performed with approximately 107 OS events (~32% maturity) observed.' But Section 9.4.1.1 says 'If PFS achieves statistical significance at the interim analysis, an administrative interim summary for OS will be performed.' - this is consistent, but the text in Section 9.2 says 'Otherwise, the OS will be assessed for superiority of AMG 510 over docetaxel at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events (~53% maturity) have been observed, whichever is later.' - this is inconsistent with Table 9-1 that says OS at PFS PA is triggered by 175 events, not 'whichever is later'.",
      "page": 104,
      "quote": "Otherwise, the OS will be assessed for superiority of AMG 510 over docetaxel at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events (~53% maturity) have been observed, whichever is later.",
      "severity": "major"
    }
  ]
}
